+-----------------------------------------------------------------------
| Running ${PKGSTEM} on OpenBSD
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------

opencode is a terminal coding agent. Run it from a project directory:

    $ opencode

Node.js ${MODNODE_DEFAULT_VERSION} or newer is required for the
TypeScript source support (--experimental-strip-types).

Self-upgrade and package-manager uninstall paths are disabled. Updates
must come from OpenBSD packages, not opencode's npm, pnpm, yarn, bun,
brew, scoop, choco, or curl upgrade paths.

Plugin support is disabled intentionally in this port. Upstream plugin
support normally depends on Bun-backed plugin and dependency handling.
Bun is not available on OpenBSD, so the port rejects plugin use instead
of trying to install, load, cache, import, or execute npm or local
plugins.

Users should not expect npm plugins, local plugins, or plugin
configuration to work. If upstream makes plugin support independent from
Bun in the future, the port can be revisited.

Zed editor selection integration is disabled in this initial port
because upstream reads Zed state through Bun's sqlite bindings.
